#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I -S
"""my-syncthing -- set up and watch a Syncthing cluster from ONE config.

The cluster config says which host is the hub, where it listens, which
devices exist and which folders go where. `--install` makes the host it runs
on match it -- Syncthing, its service, its settings, devices, folders and
ignores -- through Syncthing's own REST API; `status` and `check` report what
Syncthing actually does. It syncs nothing itself. Stdlib only: -I keeps
PYTHONPATH and the user's site out, -S skips site.
"""
